# Places of K(t) for K algebraically closed: P¹(K)

Theorem statement: `P2M.Dup.AlgebraicCurve.RationalFunctionField.eq_placeOfPoint_or_eq_placeInfty`
(`86424baf-e08f-5188-813f-e3201b47929f`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `6cfd4548-58da-5540-b323-33de1612c317`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field and let $v$ be a place of the rational function field
$\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ over $K$, that is, a term of the project structure `Place K (RatFunc K)`: a
valuation subring of $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,K$ which contains the image of $K$ under the structure map,
is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring. The conclusion is a disjunction: either there
is an element $a \in K$ with $v =$ `placeOfPoint K a`, the place attached to the irreducible
polynomial $X - C(a)$ (namely `Place.ofHeightOneSpectrum` applied to the height-one prime of $K[X]$
generated by $X - C(a)$), or $v =$ `placeInfty K`, the place whose valuation subring is the
valuation subring of `RatFunc.inftyValuation K`. Thus the places of $K(t)/K$ for $K$ algebraically
closed are exhausted by the points $a \in K$ together with the point at infinity. The statement
asserts only that this list is exhaustive; disjointness of the two cases and injectivity of $a
\mapsto$ `placeOfPoint K a` are not part of it.

This is the classification of the places of a rational function field, specialised to an
algebraically closed constant field, where the finite places correspond to the linear monic
polynomials and hence to the points of $\mathbb{A}^1(K)$, so that the full set of places is
identified with $\mathbb{P}^1(K) = K \cup \{\infty\}$. It serves as a basic tool in the
function-field part of the development, used wherever an argument proceeds by cases over all places
of $K(t)$, for instance in results on divisors, charts of annuli, and comparisons of places under
constant field extension.

